-- title:
--   A degree-seven polynomial defeats every short variation path
-- statement:
--   There exists a monic complex polynomial p of degree seven with seven distinct roots in the open unit disc such that every continuous path γ:[0,1]→ℂ joining two distinct roots and satisfying |p(γ(t))|<1 for all t∈[0,1] has extended total variation greater than 2. The witness is the fixed s=10⁻⁶ instance of ani’s construction.
